From 6b569aeb89c36b0baac86424bee8030726684f6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mik <mik@devnesthub.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:59:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix sitemap staleness: force dynamic rendering and dedupe by
 slug

The sitemap.xml route had no dynamic export, so Next.js statically
generated it once at build time (last deploy: Sep 6) and served that
same cached snapshot on every request afterward. New videos synced via
the admin panel or sync-video.ts after that deploy never appeared in
it, even though they were live on the actual site.

- app/sitemap.ts: add `export const revalidate = 0` so it queries the
  database fresh on every request, matching app/page.tsx and
  app/topic/[slug]/page.tsx, which already do this.
- app/sitemap.ts: dedupe video entries by slug defensively, so a data
  drift can never emit the same <loc> twice (this is what caused the
  omniroute-setup-connect-claude-for-free-ai-tokens-step-by-step-guide
  URL to appear twice with different lastmod dates in the live sitemap).
- lib/slugify.ts: add ensureUniqueSlug(), which checks the database
  before saving a new slug and disambiguates it if another video
  already owns it. slug is declared @unique in schema.prisma, but this
  repo has no prisma/migrations folder, so that constraint may never
  have actually been pushed to the live database, which is the most
  likely way two rows ended up sharing a slug in the first place.
- sync-video.ts / app/actions/sync.ts: call ensureUniqueSlug() before
  upserting.
- app/actions/sync.ts: also revalidatePath("/sitemap.xml") after an
  admin-triggered sync, for immediate freshness on top of revalidate=0.
---
